  "id": "Compound::DB00458 - Gene::1565",
  "verbalization": "Imipramine exhibits a strong binding interaction with Cyp2b6 and Cyp3a7, which are both involved in the metabolism of arachidonic acid and steroidogenesis, respectively. These interactions are supported by multiple paths, each showing a clear and consistent link between Imipramine and Cyp2d6 through the intermediary of arachidonic acid metabolism. The shared participation of Cyp2b6 and Cyp3a7 in arachidonic acid monooxygenase and aromatase activities, respectively, suggests that Imipramine may influence the metabolic pathways of arachidonic acid, potentially affecting steroid hormone synthesis. The recurring mechanism of binding to cytochrome P450 enzymes and their involvement in lipid metabolism underscores a plausible pathway by which Imipramine could modulate Cyp2d6 activity. The evidence is robust and consistent, supporting a mechanistic link between Imipramine and Cyp2d6 through the regulation of arachidonic acid metabolism.",
